\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Overview of the Adaptive Auto-Harness system. \emph  {Phase 1: Continual Auto-Harness} (top): between batches, a multi-agent evolver (Analyst $\to $ Researchers $\to $ Builder $\to $ Verifier) constructs and refines the harness, with persistent cross-cycle state and HITL hooks. The evolver maintains a git-backed harness tree with regime-specific branches. \emph  {Phase 2: Solve-Time Adaptation} (bottom): at solve time, agentic routing selects the most suitable branch for each task $x_t$, and the solver executes on the selected branch's workspace.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:unified_pipeline}{{2}{4}{Overview of the Adaptive Auto-Harness system. \emph {Phase 1: Continual Auto-Harness} (top): between batches, a multi-agent evolver (Analyst $\to $ Researchers $\to $ Builder $\to $ Verifier) constructs and refines the harness, with persistent cross-cycle state and HITL hooks. The evolver maintains a git-backed harness tree with regime-specific branches. \emph {Phase 2: Solve-Time Adaptation} (bottom): at solve time, agentic routing selects the most suitable branch for each task $x_t$, and the solver executes on the selected branch's workspace.\relax }{figure.caption.2}{}}
